| # | Attraction | Typical rating* | Why it’s loved | Quick‑look facts |
|---|------------|----------------|----------------|------------------|
| **1** | **Stanley Park** (urban park & waterfront) | 4.8 / 5 | Massive old‑growth forest, a 9 km seawall that’s perfect for walking/biking, free‑entry beaches, the Vancouver Aquarium, Indigenous totem poles, playgrounds and wildlife – all in the heart of the city. | • Size: ≈ 1 000 ac (405 ha)  <br>• Main spots: Seawall, English Bay, Second Beach, Brockton Point totem poles, Lost Lagoon, Vancouver Aquarium  <br>• Open: 24 h (most facilities 9 am‑5 pm)  <br>• Admission: free (Aquarium CAD 38 adult, CAD 23 child)  <br>• Best time: early morning (7‑8 am) for a quiet walk and sunrise over English Bay |
| **2** | **Capilano Suspension Bridge Park** (rain‑forest adventure) | 4.7 / 5 | A dramatic 137‑m (450‑ft) suspension bridge over the Capilano River, plus treetop walkways, a glass‑floor cliffwalk, Indigenous cultural displays and a dedicated kids‑area. The mix of thrills and natural beauty makes it a family favourite. | • Bridge length: 137 m, height: 70 m above river  <br>• Other experiences: Treetops Adventure (12 suspended bridges), Cliffwalk (glass‑floor), Indigenous cultural centre  <br>• Hours (Nov 10‑20 2024): 9 am‑5 pm (last entry 4:30 pm)  <br>• Admission: CAD 69 adult, CAD 39 child (6‑12), CAD 59 senior (65+) – online tickets 15 % cheaper  <br>• Parking: $5‑$10 /hr (or bus 236 from Lions Gate Station)  <br>• Best time: 10 am‑12 pm for good light and fewer crowds |

\*Ratings are the average of the most recent TripAdvisor, Google and local travel‑site scores (as of 2024).

